      "textEn": "It could have been ineffective, but it wasn't. On the contrary, he confessed the sin of murder.\nLaya. Later, he divided the sin among the land, water, trees and women. Because the earth accepted a quarter of sin,\nA part of the earth became a desert. The trees also accepted the same sin,\nTherefore, it sucks the juice from them, which is forbidden to drink. Women had accepted a quarter of sin,\nTherefore, they are impure during menstruation. Because water also admitted sins,\ntherefore, water that rises as bubbles cannot be used for any purpose. After the slaying of Vishwarupa, his father Tvashta performed a yajna to kill Indra. Unfortunately,\nif the mantras are pronounced irregularly, they give adverse results. It was the same with the Yajna of Tvashtri. When he was performing the Yagya for the killing of Indra, he recited a mantra for the increase of Indra's enemies.\nBut because the mantra was not recited correctly, Indra's enemy, an Asura named Vritrasura, was born.\nThe whole world was terrified by its terrifying form. In front of his personal aura, the power of the gods\nalso diminished. Seeing no way to protect themselves, all the gods, the enjoyers of the fruits of sacrifice,\njoined in the worship of the supreme, complete, and best of the entire universe, the Supreme Personality of Godhead. All the gods started worshiping him\nbecause they alone can protect living beings from fear and danger. Leaving the worship of Shri Bhagwan, taking refuge in any other deity is like crossing the ocean by holding the tail of a dog.\nIt is like crossing the ocean. A dog can swim, but that doesn't mean that by holding its tail,\nthe sea can be crossed. Pleased with the gods, Shri Bhagwan advised them to go to Dadhichi and ask for his\nbones. They will accept the prayer of the gods, and through their ashes, Vritrasura can be killed.\nIt will be possible. Sreeshuka said"
